        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mario Mazzacurati, Ettore Bugatti\n- Companies: Automobiles Ettore Bugatti\n- Places: South Africa, Molsheim, Alsace\n- Roles: engineer, auto racer driver\n- Products: Bugatti cars\n- Events: 1936 South African Grand Prix\n\nFacts:\n- Automobiles Ettore Bugatti was founded in 1909 in the then German city of Molsheim, Alsace, by Italian-born Ettore Bugatti.\n- Mario Mazzacurati was born on 21 October 1903 and later became an Italian engineer and auto racer driver active in South Africa.\n- Mario Mazzacurati won the 1936 South African Grand Prix driving Bugatti cars under the pseudonym Mario Massacuratti.\n- Mario Mazzacurati died on 17 April 1985.",
